/*******************************************************************************
 * CHIP:  BCM_APERTA2_ID
 * REGISTER:  SYS_PMIF_PMIF_ERR_INTR_STATUS
 * BLOCKS:   SYS_PMIF
 * REGADDR:  0x200e
 * DESC:     PMIF register bridge error intr status
 * RESETVAL: 0x0 (0)
 * ACCESS:   R/W
 * FIELDS:
 *     INTR_LMI_PM_ERR  latch high error in case pmif is asserting an error to lmi
 *     INTR_LMI_SBUS_ERROR Latched high status of bus_error signal in recived sbus opcode,If this bit is high then lmi_err is expected from PMIF
 *     INTR_DLEN_ERR    When set, it indicates an DLEN error from PM SBUS opcode and recived  dlen from PM does'nt match with orignal lmi transaction.If this bit is high then lmi_err is expected from PMIFbuffer.Clear on read field
 *     INTR_PM_RESET_ERR When set, it indicates LMI is trying to access PM regs/memory while PM OOR is not set to 1(PM is in reset).If this bit is high then lmi_err is expected from PMIFbuffer.Clear on read field
 *     INTR_DC3MAC_RESET_ERR When set, it indicates LMI is trying to access dc3mac regs/memory while cdmac1 OOR is not set to 1(PM is in reset). If this bit is high then lmi_err is expected from PMIFbuffer.Clear on read field
 *     INTR_TSC_RESET_ERR When set, it indicates LMI is trying to access tsc regs/memory while tsc OOR is not set to 1(PM is in reset).If this bit is high then lmi_err is expected from PMIFbuffer.Clear on read field
 *     INTR_DPORT_ID_ERR When set, it indicates an DPORT id programed inn strap_port_blkid_frcval doesnt match with incoming PM SBUS Opcode DPORT Id.If this bit is high then lmi_err is expected from PMIFbuffer.Clear on read field
 *     INTR_OPCODE_NO_ACK When set, it indicates that incoming PM SBUS Opcode is diffrent then expected rd_ack or wr_ack.If this bit is high then lmi_err is expected from PMIFbuffer.Clear on read field
 *     INTR_WDOG_EXPIRE When set, it indicates that wtachdog timer expired and either no PM SBUS Opcode or a wrong Pm opcode is recived .If this bit is high then lmi_err is expected from PMIFbuffer.Clear on read field
 *
 ******************************************************************************/
